# Phase-Wise Implementation Plan v2: Google Photos Discovery Engine

Revision of the original plan. Changes are marked **[FIX]**. Numeric targets are proposed starting points; set them after measuring a baseline on the golden set.

## Decisions to lock before coding

| Topic | Decision |
|---|---|
| Structured output | Let `instructor` own the JSON mode. Do not also set `response_format` by hand. |
| Clustering library | Use `sklearn.cluster.HDBSCAN` (scikit-learn >= 1.3). Drop the standalone `hdbscan` package. |
| Frontend | One stack: Vite + React + Recharts, built to static files and hosted on **Vercel**. No Next.js server. FastAPI does not serve the frontend. |
| Backend hosting | **Railway**, deployed from a Dockerfile (CPU-only PyTorch, embedding model baked into the image). |
| Secrets | All third-party keys (Groq, Supabase service key, API key) live only in Railway variables. The browser never receives a secret. |
| Gap labels | Each review gets a `primary_gap` and an optional `secondary_gap`. |
| "Funnel" | Rename to **Failure Distribution**. One label per review is a distribution, not stage-to-stage drop-off. |
| Model IDs | Read from config/env, never hardcoded. Check Groq's current model list and limits (RPM, TPM and daily caps) before Phase 3. |
| Stage numbering | Stage 1 Ingest, 2 Sanitize, 3 Filter, 4 Extract, 5 Classify, 6 Cluster, 7 Synthesize, 8 Top Issues. |

