## Open questions

1. Multilingual reviews: Out of scope or switch to multilingual?
Decision: Strictly Out of Scope (English Only).

PM Rationale: Switching to a multilingual embedding model introduces noise and complexity into the HDBSCAN clustering parameters. For an MVP demonstrating the "Anatomy of Memory," English reviews provide more than enough signal. Add a simple filter to drop non-English text and document this constraint in your limitations slide.

2. Is this personal/academic, or will it be shared publicly?
Decision: Academic / Portfolio Use.

PM Rationale: You are building this to showcase product-sense and technical orchestration for your fellowship and future roles. Because you are not commercializing the insights or monetizing the traffic, scraping public app stores and Reddit falls comfortably under fair use for academic/research purposes.

3. Chat retrieval: pgvector in Supabase, or in-memory embeddings?
Decision: In-Memory Embeddings.

PM Rationale: Do not spend your final hours configuring pgvector extensions in Supabase. At your target volume (1,000–2,000 reviews), storing embeddings in memory as a simple NumPy array or Pandas dataframe will consume less than 50MB of RAM. A local cosine-similarity search using scikit-learn or numpy will execute in milliseconds. Keep the infrastructure lean.

4. Protecting /pipeline/run and /chat: Vercel serverless proxy or Supabase Auth?
Decision: Vercel Serverless Proxy (with a server-side key).

PM Rationale: Implementing Supabase Auth requires setting up login screens, handling session tokens, and managing user states in React. That is a massive distraction. Instead, create a simple Vercel serverless function (frontend/api/run.js) that injects a hidden process.env.API_SECRET before forwarding the request to your Railway backend. This secures the endpoint in less than 10 lines of code.

5. Should the dashboard be public, or restricted?
Decision: 100% Public (Read-Only).

PM Rationale: Evaluators face immense friction if forced to log in or request access. The dashboard UI should be globally accessible so anyone clicking the link in your slide deck instantly sees the insights. Only the execution endpoints (/api/pipeline/run and /api/chat) should be locked behind the proxy key.